          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ker
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{n+1} \coloneqq C[\ker F_n^{-1}]
          %p
            Now consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ω
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_\omega \,\coloneqq\, \colim_n C_n
          %p
            of this sequence of localizations. Clearly there is a canonical functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon C \to C_\omega
            and also a mediating map
          #eq:MediatingMap.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \,\colon\, C_\omega \to D
          %p
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\circ L = F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
              is an
              %strong iterated localization
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MediatingMap"} (1)
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
          %p
            This makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mtext iterated localizations
                  %mo ,
                  %mtext conservative functors
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big(\text{iterated localizations}, \text{conservative functors}\big)
            a(n homotopy)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Cat}
            (considered as a 1-category with weak equivalences given by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalences of categories
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"}> localization of a category
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+systems"} orthogonal factorization systems
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative functor
          %h2#references References
          %p The above is pretty much directly taken from:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal"}> Joyal
                ‘s CatLab, Ex. 6.12 in:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Factorisation+systems"} Factorisation systems
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                , §11.14 and pp. 70 in:
                %em Notes on quasi-categories
                (2008) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/IMA/Joyal.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalNotesOnQuasiCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
